<%- include('../partials/admin-top', { title }) %>

<h1>Reports &amp; status</h1>
<p class="sub">Service status shown to users, plus how and when the bot reports back to you on Telegram.</p>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Service status</h2>
  <form method="post" action="/admin/reports/service">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="status">Status (shown in /status and the portal)</label>
        <select id="status" name="status">
          <option value="operational" <%= s.serviceStatus === 'operational' ? 'selected' : '' %>>✅ Operational</option>
          <option value="degraded" <%= s.serviceStatus === 'degraded' ? 'selected' : '' %>>⚠️ Degraded / issues</option>
          <option value="maintenance" <%= s.serviceStatus === 'maintenance' ? 'selected' : '' %>>🛠 Maintenance</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="note">Note (optional, e.g. "server move, back at 20:00 UTC")</label>
        <input id="note" name="note" type="text" maxlength="300" value="<%= s.serviceNote %>">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="announceChanges" name="announceChanges" value="1" <%= s.announceChanges ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="announceChanges">Auto-announce status changes to the group</label>
    </div>
    <p><button type="submit">Update status</button></p>
  </form>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Telegram reporting</h2>
  <form method="post" action="/admin/reports/settings">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
    <label for="adminTelegramIds">Admin Telegram user IDs (comma separated)</label>
    <input id="adminTelegramIds" name="adminTelegramIds" type="text" value="<%= s.adminTelegramIds %>" placeholder="123456789, 987654321">
    <p class="hint">Get your ID by messaging <code>@userinfobot</code> on Telegram. Each admin must also send the bot a /start DM once (Telegram rule: bots can't DM first). These IDs can also use admin commands like /adopt, /report and /broadcast.</p>

    <h2>Instant alerts</h2>
    <div class="checkline"><input type="checkbox" id="alertErrors" name="alertErrors" value="1" <%= s.alertErrors ? 'checked' : '' %>><label for="alertErrors">Bot errors and AI endpoint failures</label></div>
    <div class="checkline"><input type="checkbox" id="alertBudget" name="alertBudget" value="1" <%= s.alertBudget ? 'checked' : '' %>><label for="alertBudget">Daily AI budget reached</label></div>
    <div class="checkline"><input type="checkbox" id="alertProblems" name="alertProblems" value="1" <%= s.alertProblems ? 'checked' : '' %>><label for="alertProblems">Problem reports in the group (buffering, channels down…) — batched, with outage detection</label></div>
    <div class="checkline"><input type="checkbox" id="alertBannedWords" name="alertBannedWords" value="1" <%= s.alertBannedWords ? 'checked' : '' %>><label for="alertBannedWords">Banned-word triggers</label></div>
    <div class="checkline"><input type="checkbox" id="alertVod" name="alertVod" value="1" <%= s.alertVod ? 'checked' : '' %>><label for="alertVod">VOD requests ("Request: Title") — also listed in <a href="/admin/requests">VOD requests</a></label></div>

    <h2>Automatic degradation</h2>
    <p class="hint">When this many <strong>different people</strong> report service-wide problems (buffering, streams not loading, login failures) within the window, the service status flips to <em>degraded</em> automatically. Reporters then get told it's a known issue rather than being walked through fixes that can't help, and you get a DM. Complaints about a single episode or movie never count. The status clears itself once reports stop; a status you set by hand is never touched.</p>
    <p class="hint"><strong>Nothing is posted to your group automatically.</strong> The threshold is a heuristic, and a false positive would put "we have an outage" in front of paying customers with nobody checking — so the DM carries an <strong>Announce to the group</strong> button instead, and the all-clear works the same way.</p>
    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="degradeThreshold">People reporting (0 = off)</label>
        <input id="degradeThreshold" name="degradeThreshold" type="number" min="0" max="50" value="<%= s.degradeThreshold %>">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="degradeWindowMinutes">Within (minutes)</label>
        <input id="degradeWindowMinutes" name="degradeWindowMinutes" type="number" min="5" max="120" value="<%= s.degradeWindowMinutes %>">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="degradeRecoverMinutes">Auto-clear after quiet (minutes)</label>
        <input id="degradeRecoverMinutes" name="degradeRecoverMinutes" type="number" min="5" max="720" value="<%= s.degradeRecoverMinutes %>">
      </div>
    </div>

    <label for="announceMessage">Announcement text (empty = never offer to announce)</label>
    <input id="announceMessage" name="announceMessage" type="text" maxlength="1000" value="<%= s.announceMessage %>">
    <p class="hint"><code>{note}</code> becomes the bot's own summary of what people are reporting, e.g. "We're seeing several reports of buffering problems and are looking into it."</p>

    <label for="recoveredMessage">All-clear text</label>
    <input id="recoveredMessage" name="recoveredMessage" type="text" maxlength="1000" value="<%= s.recoveredMessage %>">
    <p class="hint">Offered when the status clears itself, so the group hears it's fixed rather than being left wondering.</p>

    <h2>AI digest</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="digest">Schedule</label>
        <select id="digest" name="digest">
          <option value="off" <%= s.digest === 'off' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Off</option>
          <option value="daily" <%= s.digest === 'daily' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Daily</option>
          <option value="weekly" <%= s.digest === 'weekly' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Weekly (Mondays)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="digestHour">Send at (hour, UTC)</label>
        <input id="digestHour" name="digestHour" type="number" min="0" max="23" value="<%= s.digestHour %>">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="expiryReminderDays">Customer expiry reminder (days before)</label>
        <input id="expiryReminderDays" name="expiryReminderDays" type="number" min="1" max="30" value="<%= s.expiryReminderDays %>">
      </div>
    </div>

    <label for="expiryReminderMessage">Reminder DM before expiry ({name}, {days} — empty = off)</label>
    <input id="expiryReminderMessage" name="expiryReminderMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.expiryReminderMessage %>">

    <label for="expiryUpsellMessage">Win-back DM on expiry day ({name} — empty = off)</label>
    <input id="expiryUpsellMessage" name="expiryUpsellMessage" type="text" maxlength="500" value="<%= s.expiryUpsellMessage %>">
    <p class="hint">Sent once when a linked customer's access lapses (never for accounts expired more than 3 days). Only customers who have DMed the bot can receive it.</p>

    <div class="checkline">
      <input type="checkbox" id="suggestFaqs" name="suggestFaqs" value="1" <%= s.suggestFaqs ? 'checked' : '' %>>
      <label for="suggestFaqs">Weekly AI-drafted FAQ suggestions from unanswered questions (review in <a href="/admin/faqs">FAQs</a>)</label>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
      <div>
        <label for="retentionDays">Keep message stats for (days)</label>
        <input id="retentionDays" name="retentionDays" type="number" min="1" max="365" value="<%= s.retentionDays %>">
      </div>
    </div>
    <p><button type="submit">Save reporting settings</button></p>
  </form>
  <div class="toolbar">
    <form method="post" action="/admin/reports/test-alert">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
      <button class="btn-ghost btn-sm" <%= botOnline ? '' : 'disabled' %>>Send test alert</button>
    </form>
    <form method="post" action="/admin/reports/send-digest">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
      <button class="btn-ghost btn-sm">Generate digest now</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Recent digests</h2>
  <% if (!digests.length) { %><p class="hint">No digests yet — enable the schedule or hit "Generate digest now".</p><% } %>
  <% for (const d of digests) { %>
  <div style="margin-bottom:16px">
    <div class="hint"><%= formatDate(d.created_at) %> · <%= d.period %></div>
    <pre class="mono"><%= d.body %></pre>
  </div>
  <% } %>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/admin-bottom') %>
